    <Program class="ca.nrcan.gc.OEE.ERS.ErsProgram">
        <Labels>
            <English>EnerGuide Rating System</English>
            <French>SystÃ¨me de cote ÃnerGuide</French>
        </Labels>
        <Version major="15" minor="1" build="19">
            <Labels>
                <English>v15.1b19</English>
                <French>v15.1b19</French>
            </Labels>
        </Version>
        <SdkVersion major="1" minor="11">
            <Labels>
                <English>v1.11</English>
                <French>v1.11</French>
            </Labels>
        </SdkVersion>
        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="true" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="true" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="3">
                    <English>No Vermiculite</English>
                    <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <HouseholdOperatingConditions numberOfOccupants="2" coolingSeasonMonths="4" isClothesWasherEnergySaver="false" isLightingEnergySaver="true" areAppliancesEnergySaver="false">
                <Thermostat heatingDaytime="20" heatingNighttime="20" cooling="25" />
            </HouseholdOperatingConditions>
            <AtypicalElectricalLoads deIcingCables="false" exteriorLighting="false" hotTub="false" heatedGarage="true" portableAirConditioning="false" pool="false" mixedUse="false" totalUnits="0" energyStarUnits="0" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>Air Leakage Areas: Back door, windows in kitchen and basement, electrical outlets, door to garage, basement headers in crawl space.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>The main walls are losing lots of heat so they should have more insulation added to them. Adding a minimum 2" of rigid board insulation (R-10 value) would help with heat loss. There are incentives for upgrading your walls from Energy Solutions Centre. If you upgrade the walls with a nominal insualtion value between R-10 and R-19 you will receive $0.50/square foot. For upgrades of R-20 nominal insualtion value of R-20 or higher, you will receive $2.50/square foot.  It is required to have 20% of the area of  the walls upgraded to receive the rebate.</mainWalls>
                <exposedFloors>I assumed there is R-12 batt insulation in the floor above the garage. If you ever plan on doing any renovations it would be a good  idea to check and see what is actually in the floor for insulation. The floors are assumed to be 2x10 as the floor above the crawl space is 2x10. You could add an R-31 batt or 5-6" of spray foam to the exposed floor above the garage if you ever decide to renovate.</exposedFloors>
                <foundation>The foundation walls should be upgraded. The crawl space should have a 2 x 8 wall built in front of the concrete. The current situation where the insulation is just against the wall is still allowing air to leak into the home and heat to escape. The exterior of the foundation wall should have 2" of rigid board insualtion added to it. The foundation floor should also have 1-2" of rigid board insulation added to it to help with heat loss. You may not want to add to the floor though as you could lose height in the basement The headers in the crawl space is a bad air leakage area. The headers should have 4-5" of spray foam in them to properly air seal and insualted the space. The same incentives/rebates as walls will apply to header areas, foundation walls, and floor joists.</foundation>
                <windows>The older windows in the basement and in the kitchen should be replaced with Energy Star windows rated for climate zone 3. There are rebates available from the Energy Solutions Centre for $100 per new window installed.</windows>
                <doors>The bottom seal on the back door is not working properly. The door is old and is in need of an upgrade as well.The back door should be replaced with a steel door with a medium density spray foam fill. The door to the garage should also be replaced and properly air sealed. There is a rebate available from the Energy Solutions Centre for $100 if a new door is installed.</doors>
                <VentilationSystem>Adding a HRV will improve the air quality inside the home. There is a $500 rebate available from the Energy Solutions Centre. The HRV must have a sensible recovery effectiveness of 64% or higher at -25 degrees celcius design temperature.</VentilationSystem>
                <HotWaterSystem>The hot and cold water pipes in the furnace room should be insulated to prevent  heat loss and condensation.</HotWaterSystem>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
